WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:20.473
About a month later, Dr. Dolittle reached Puddleby.

2
00:00:20.474 --> 00:00:26.127
"Puddleby! It's good to be home!" the doctor let out a long sigh.

3
00:00:26.128 --> 00:00:29.506
"Home sweet home!" shouted Gub-Gub.

4
00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:35.620
"I can't wait to see everyone," Dab-Dab said excitedly.

5
00:00:35.621 --> 00:00:38.180
They walked slowly back to the house.

6
00:00:38.181 --> 00:00:41.693
"Everything looks the same," remarked Gub-Gub.

7
00:00:41.694 --> 00:00:45.838
"Puddleby will never change," added Dr. Dolittle.

8
00:00:45.839 --> 00:00:52.179
"Dr. Dolittle?" A horse pulled his glasses closer.

9
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:57.373
"Oh, hello! How are you?" the doctor asked pleasantly.

10
00:00:57.374 --> 00:00:59.987
The horse could not speak for a while.

11
00:00:59.988 --> 00:01:03.767
"We thought you left Puddleby!" he finally said.

12
00:01:03.768 --> 00:01:15.794
"No, no. We went on a . . . ," Dr. Dolittle paused, "an adventure."

13
00:01:15.795 --> 00:01:18.096
Finally, they arrived at the house.

14
00:01:18.097 --> 00:01:23.192
"Welcome to your new home," the doctor said to the pushmi-pullyu.

15
00:01:23.193 --> 00:01:27.565
"Thank you. It's very nice," the creature replied.

16
00:01:27.566 --> 00:01:30.726
Suddenly the doors opened.

17
00:01:30.727 --> 00:01:37.939
"Dr. Dolittle! Dr. Dolittle!" shouted all the animals that had stayed behind.

18
00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:42.671
Dr. Dolittle spent hours telling them about the trip.

19
00:01:42.672 --> 00:01:48.019
"Psst! What's that?" the cow whispered to Dab-Dab.

20
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:54.161
"That's the pushmi-pullyu, the rarest animal in the world," the duck answered.

21
00:01:54.162 --> 00:01:57.814
"It's got two heads!" the rabbit said too loudly.

22
00:01:57.815 --> 00:02:03.431
"SSSHHH!" the other animals said to the rabbit.

23
00:02:03.432 --> 00:02:08.763
Before long, everyone in Puddleby heard of Dr. Dolittle's return.

24
00:02:08.764 --> 00:02:12.889
They also heard he brought a two-headed animal from Africa.

25
00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:18.443
Dr. Dolittle put up a sign that read, "The rarest animal in the world!

26
00:02:18.444 --> 00:02:22.765
Look but don't touch!"

27
00:02:22.766 --> 00:02:26.610
At first the pushmi-pullyu was very uncomfortable.

28
00:02:26.611 --> 00:02:30.094
But soon he didn't mind people looking at him.

29
00:02:30.095 --> 00:02:33.101
People from the circus wanted to buy him.

30
00:02:33.102 --> 00:02:35.343
"See?" said Dab-Dab.

31
00:02:35.344 --> 00:02:39.339
"Everybody wants you!"

32
00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.168
Dr. Dolittle didn't want more money.

33
00:02:42.169 --> 00:02:44.090
He had more than enough.

34
00:02:44.091 --> 00:02:47.741
"Money," he sighed, "what a headache.

35
00:02:47.742 --> 00:02:51.481
But it's nice not to have to worry."

36
00:02:51.482 --> 00:02:55.948
Dr. Dolittle visited the sailor who had given him the boat.

37
00:02:55.949 --> 00:02:59.950
"I'm sorry about your boat," he apologized.

38
00:02:59.951 --> 00:03:03.094
The kind sailor said, "That's okay, Doctor.

39
00:03:03.095 --> 00:03:05.191
I'm glad you're home safely."

40
00:03:05.192 --> 00:03:09.735
But then the doctor surprised him.

41
00:03:09.736 --> 00:03:14.492
Dr. Dolittle gave the sailor not one, but two boats.

42
00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:17.018
One of them was the Barbary ship.

43
00:03:17.019 --> 00:03:20.570
"Oh, thank you so much!" cried the sailor.

44
00:03:20.571 --> 00:03:28.540
"Without your help, we could never have gone to Africa," Dr. Dolittle shook the sailor's hand.

45
00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:31.788
Dr. Dolittle also bought a new piano.

46
00:03:31.789 --> 00:03:38.692
"Now you can move out of my drawers," he told the happy mice, "and back inside the piano."

47
00:03:38.693 --> 00:03:44.571
Every day was filled with joy, now that Dr. Dolittle was back.

48
00:03:44.572 --> 00:03:48.732
Dr. Dolittle continued to take care of other people's animals.

49
00:03:48.733 --> 00:03:52.129
But he was happiest at home with his pets.

50
00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:57.127
Every night the kind animal doctor fell asleep smiling to himself.

51
00:03:57.128 --> 00:04:10.550
And every night he dreamt about his next adventure.

52
00:04:10.551 --> 00:05:16.405
[caption_out@
